pamsignal (0.5.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Feature: new `enable_notification_type` config key — comma-separated
    list of event categories (`login_success`, `login_failed`,
    `session_open`, `session_close`, `brute_force`, or `all`) that
    selects which categories produce chat alerts (#22, requested by
    @huy-lv). Default is `all`, so existing deployments behave
    unchanged. Filter only gates chat dispatch
    (Telegram / Slack / Teams / WhatsApp / Discord / custom webhook);
    `journalctl -t pamsignal` still records every event, preserving
    the forensic trail. Unknown tokens, empty values, and empty list
    elements are hard config errors. The existing per-event
    suppression for sudo/su LOGIN_FAILED is unchanged and layered
    beneath this filter.
  * Security (examples): bump `idna` 3.14 -> 3.15 in
    `examples/python-webhook/uv.lock` (Dependabot alert #1,
    CVE-2026-45409, CVSS 6.9). `idna < 3.15` is vulnerable to a DoS
    when `idna.encode()` is called with crafted long inputs; the
    length-rejection check ran after `valid_contexto`, reopening the
    gap CVE-2024-3651 was supposed to close. PAMSignal itself is C
    and unaffected; the alert fires only on the example Flask
    receiver's transitive dep via `requests`. Lockfile-only refresh.
  * Security (examples): bump `qs` 6.14.2 / 6.15.1 -> 6.15.2 in
    `examples/nodejs-webhook/pnpm-lock.yaml` (Dependabot alert #2,
    CVE-2026-8723, CVSS 6.3). `qs >= 6.11.1, <= 6.15.1` throws
    `TypeError` synchronously when `stringify` is called with
    `arrayFormat: 'comma'` and `encodeValuesOnly: true` on an array
    containing `null`/`undefined`. PAMSignal itself is C and
    unaffected; the alert fires only on the example Express
    receiver's transitive `qs`. Pinned via pnpm `overrides` so both
    6.14.2 (express 4.x) and 6.15.1 (body-parser / formidable)
    collapse to the patched 6.15.2.
  * Docs: README acknowledgments corrected — Hong Quan (not "Hong
    Quang"), FHS contribution (not ECS). Avatars added.

