pamsignal (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * BREAKING (revert of v0.3.0 path move): daemon binary moves
    from /usr/sbin/pamsignal back to /usr/bin/pamsignal to align
    with the systemd-era convention that admin-oriented commands
    (journalctl, systemctl, podman, containerd) all ship in
    /usr/bin despite being administrator tools. Fedora 42+
    has formally retired the bin/sbin split; Debian Trixie has
    the merge on its roadmap. v0.3.0's FHS-§4.10 reading is
    historically valid but on the wrong side of where the
    ecosystem is moving. dpkg handles the relocation atomically
    on upgrade and the unit's ExecStart is updated in lockstep
    via meson configure_file. Anyone who scripted against the
    /usr/sbin/pamsignal path that v0.3.0 introduced for ~30
    minutes needs to revert to /usr/bin/pamsignal.

